{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2cYjPB4Bp72HEmhqbp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the race in `metrics/counter.py`. `tests/test_metrics.py` passed 5 out of 5 runs after the change. I did not run it against the original code to confirm it failed there before the fix.\n\n**Root cause:** `incr` did an unlocked read-modify-write on a shared dict, so concurrent increments overwrote each other. `snapshot()` copied that dict while other threads were inserting new keys, which could produce a copy taken mid-update.\n\n**Fix:** Each counter name now maps to a small `_Cell` object with its own lock.\n- `incr` takes only that counter's lock, so different counters don't contend.\n- A short registry lock guards the name-to-cell mapping (lookups, inserts, removals).\n- `snapshot()` holds the registry lock while building a plain `dict` of name to value, so the copy never sees a mid-insert dict.\n- `get`, `reset`, and the public API are unchanged.\n\n**Trade-offs:**\n- `snapshot()` is consistent per counter, not across counters. Two counters read at slightly different moments can be inconsistent with each other. That matches the old semantics; it was never a transaction.\n- If `reset(name)` runs while an `incr` on that name is in flight, the in-flight increment can be discarded. It is equivalent to the increment having happened just before the reset.\n- I kept the `time.sleep(0)` inside the per-counter lock, so the test still exercises the read-to-write window.\n\nI did not commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7020,"cache_read_input_tokens":30813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7020},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1dfa1f46-c495-4b7a-9b55-424844d20659","uuid":"162bfc06-3e5c-4896-ab3f-dbafcc6aa894","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:06:19.898Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs2cYQHSiugp6KqUdR8E"}
